From 06bfcdec6f703f88577a8d0f889adb2a121ebe90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rams95 <rams95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:46:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0018-native-options-line-jp-live-walk-speed.patch

The game's own Options list (from the title and from the in-game menu's Options tab) gets a PC settings line in place of
'Adjust screen position' (PS2_NATIVE_ROW): the game's cursor (found by the list's table pointer), its help line rewritten in
the game's text, Cross opens the PC settings in the screen's look. The Japanese pictures (overrides under jp/) switch at
once with the in-game switch (ps2::set_jp_textures, PS2_JP_TEXTURES). Readable key names in the game's texts (LMB, RMB,
Spc, Ent...), key caps sized to the game's font, no key card. F6 held: fast forward. The mouse wheel sets the walk speed of
the walk keys (5 steps) when no button has the wheel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
